Subject: [Rpy] rpy2-2.2.0alpha3
Message-ID: <4D5E15D5.9010305@gmail.com>

Hi,

A tag PRERELEASE_2_2_0_ALPHA3 has been created in the branch 
version_2.2.x of the bitbucket repository.

Because of an accumulation of small inconveniences, direct (such as 
hardware failure on a development machine) or indirect, the schedule for 
the beta at https://bitbucket.org/lgautier/rpy2/wiki/Roadmap is becoming 
unrealistic. Rpy2 is currently about one month being schedule.

The alpha3 is rather stable at runtime and thanks to Thomas Kluyver 
constant attention and patches Python 3 support is not drifting behind.. 
Instability is mostly around changes in the API still to be made.

People using rpy2 interactively (bpython, idle, ipython, or else) will 
want to try out the new features outlined at 
http://rpy.sourceforge.net/rpy2/doc-2.2/html/interactive.html .



Laurent

